<section class="section">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="contact-grid">
      <div>
        <span class="section-label">What you actually get</span>
        <h2 class="section-title" style="max-width:24ch">A five-point report you can act on, even without me.</h2>
        <p>Most "free audits" are sales decks dressed up as audits. This is the opposite. The deliverable is a written report (PDF or email) that names specific issues, ranks them by impact, and tells you exactly what to do about each one. If the answer is "your site is fine, do not hire me," that is also a possible outcome.</p>

        <h3 style="margin-top:2rem;font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:1.15rem">The five points</h3>
        <ol style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:0.85rem;list-style:none;counter-reset:audit-num;padding:0;margin-top:1rem">
          <li style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:36px 1fr;gap:0.85rem;align-items:flex-start;font-size:0.95rem;line-height:1.6;counter-increment:audit-num">
            <span style="width:32px;height:32px;background:var(--navy-900);color:var(--gold-400);border-radius:50%;display:inline-flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-family:var(--font-display);font-weight:700;font-size:0.95rem">1</span>
            <span><strong>Speed.</strong> Real-world Google PageSpeed numbers (mobile + desktop), Core Web Vitals, biggest blocking files. I tell you what is slow, why, and how much of a search-ranking penalty you are paying.</span>
          </li>
          <li style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:36px 1fr;gap:0.85rem;align-items:flex-start;font-size:0.95rem;line-height:1.6;counter-increment:audit-num">
            <span style="width:32px;height:32px;background:var(--navy-900);color:var(--gold-400);border-radius:50%;display:inline-flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-family:var(--font-display);font-weight:700;font-size:0.95rem">2</span>
            <span><strong>Mobile experience.</strong> Most of your customers find you on a phone. I look at the site at 360px (small phone) and 768px (tablet) and report layout breaks, tap-target failures, and form usability issues.</span>
          </li>
          <li style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:36px 1fr;gap:0.85rem;align-items:flex-start;font-size:0.95rem;line-height:1.6;counter-increment:audit-num">
            <span style="width:32px;height:32px;background:var(--navy-900);color:var(--gold-400);border-radius:50%;display:inline-flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-family:var(--font-display);font-weight:700;font-size:0.95rem">3</span>
            <span><strong>Local SEO foundation.</strong> Title tags, meta descriptions, schema, NAP consistency, sitemap submission. I cross-check what is on the site against what is on your Google Business Profile and flag mismatches.</span>
          </li>
          <li style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:36px 1fr;gap:0.85rem;align-items:flex-start;font-size:0.95rem;line-height:1.6;counter-increment:audit-num">
            <span style="width:32px;height:32px;background:var(--navy-900);color:var(--gold-400);border-radius:50%;display:inline-flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-family:var(--font-display);font-weight:700;font-size:0.95rem">4</span>
            <span><strong>Accessibility.</strong> WCAG 2.2 AA spot-check using <a href="https://wave.webaim.org" rel="noopener" class="inline-link">WAVE</a> and Lighthouse. I report contrast failures, missing labels, keyboard traps. ADA-compliance lawsuits against small business sites are real and rising.</span>
          </li>
          <li style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:36px 1fr;gap:0.85rem;align-items:flex-start;font-size:0.95rem;line-height:1.6;counter-increment:audit-num">
            <span style="width:32px;height:32px;background:var(--navy-900);color:var(--gold-400);border-radius:50%;display:inline-flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-family:var(--font-display);font-weight:700;font-size:0.95rem">5</span>
            <span><strong>Conversion path.</strong> Where is the phone number on every page? How many clicks to a contact form? Is the call-to-action visible above the fold on mobile? The path from visitor to call should be obvious; I tell you where yours breaks.</span>
          </li>
        </ol>

        <div style="margin-top:2.5rem;padding:1.5rem 1.75rem;background:var(--bg-alt);border-left:3px solid var(--gold-500);border-radius:0 var(--radius-sm) var(--radius-sm) 0">
          <h3 style="font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:1.05rem;font-weight:600;margin-bottom:0.65rem">Why is this free?</h3>
          <p style="margin:0;font-size:0.92rem;line-height:1.65">Two reasons. (1) Most service-business owners have never seen a real website audit and do not know what their site is worth fixing. The audit gives you that picture. (2) About one in five audit recipients hires me afterwards. The other four get a useful report to share with whoever does maintain their site. Both outcomes are fine with me.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="contact-form-card">
        <h2 class="form-heading">Request your audit</h2>
        <p class="form-intro">Five fields. Five business days for the report.</p>

        <form id="auditForm" data-web3forms data-redirect="/thank-you/?type=audit" action="https://api.web3forms.com/submit" method="POST" class="form">
          <input type="hidden" name="access_key" value="b6c3454b-f07c-43f7-9070-0e0cb5286f55">
          <input type="hidden" name="subject" value="New audit request, Pikes Peak Web Designs">
          <input type="hidden" name="from_name" value="Pikes Peak Web Designs">
          <input type="checkbox" name="botcheck" style="display:none" tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off">

          <div class="form-group">
            <label for="auditName">Your name <span class="req">*</span></label>
            <input type="text" id="auditName" name="name" placeholder="Jane Smith" required autocomplete="name">
          </div>

          <div class="form-group">
            <label for="auditBusiness">Business name <span class="req">*</span></label>
            <input type="text" id="auditBusiness" name="business" placeholder="Smith's Roofing" required autocomplete="organization">
          </div>

          <div class="form-group">
            <label for="auditEmail">Email <span class="req">*</span></label>
            <input type="email" id="auditEmail" name="email" placeholder="jane@yourbusiness.com" required autocomplete="email">
          </div>

          <div class="form-group">
            <label for="auditUrl">Your website URL <span class="req">*</span></label>
            <input type="url" id="auditUrl" name="website" placeholder="https://yourbusiness.com" required>
          </div>

          <div class="form-group">
            <label for="auditConcern">What is the one thing about your site that concerns you most?</label>
            <textarea id="auditConcern" name="concern" placeholder="Slow on phones? Not showing up on Google? Form does not work? Outdated look? Whatever it is, mention it here." rows="3"></textarea>
          </div>

          <div id="form-error" role="alert" class="form-error">
            Something went wrong. Please try again or email me directly at <a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">{{ site.email }}</a>.
          </div>

          <button type="submit" class="btn btn-primary btn-full btn-lg">Send my audit request</button>
          <p class="form-hint">Free. No obligation. <a href="/privacy-policy/" class="inline-link">Privacy policy</a>.</p>
        </form>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section--cream">
  <div class="container" style="max-width:760px">
    <div class="text-center">
      <span class="section-label">Common questions</span>
      <h2 class="section-title" style="margin-inline:auto">Quick answers about the audit.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="faq-list" style="margin-top:2rem;text-align:left">
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">Is it really free? <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">Yes. No card, no credit pulled, no "after the audit" surprise charge. The audit is the audit.</div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">How long does it take to get the report? <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">Five business days from when you submit. Usually faster. If I am unusually backed up I will email you with an updated estimate.</div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">Do I have to be on a sales call to get it? <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">No. The report comes by email as a PDF or a Loom video walkthrough, your choice. If you want to talk through it afterwards, that is a separate (still free) call.</div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">What if my site is on Wix / Squarespace / WordPress? <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">Doesn't matter for the audit. I evaluate the live site, not the platform. If the platform is part of the problem I will say so, but the audit covers what visitors actually experience regardless of how the site was built.</div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">Will you try to sell me a new website? <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">If your site has issues I cannot fix without rebuilding, I will say so honestly &mdash; that is part of the report. If your site is fine, I will say that too. About one in five audits leads to a build engagement; the other four do not, and that is OK.</div></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

